Fix the DevStyle theme falling apart on Eclipse 2026-09 (4.41): the base
stylesheets fail to load because their relative @import rules can no longer
be resolved.

DevStyle's themes are served through its own devstyle: URL scheme
(devstyle://css/linux.css etc.; the handler substitutes the active color
theme into the CSS). Each base stylesheet starts with relative imports such
as @import url("include/basestyle.css"). When the e4 engine resolves such an
import it first tries the stylesheet's own directory and, if that is not a
plain file, asks the registered resource locators; the stock engine then
does new URL(resolve(href)) without a null check. Up to 4.40 DevStyle's
CSSEngineFixer weaver replaced that engine method with a copy that guards
the null and falls back to the devstyle: URL. Eclipse 4.41 rewrote the CSS
core (AbstractCSSEngine and the SAC DOM are gone), the weaver finds nothing
to weave, and every DevStyle base stylesheet dies with
"MalformedURLException: Cannot invoke String.length() because spec is null"
in ThemeEngine.setTheme — three times per start — leaving the workbench with
thin borders and system-theme backgrounds (revstyle issue #7).

Declare an OSGi resource locator for the bundle's css/ folder on the
stylesheet element theming.css already contributes. The ThemeEngine registers
locators from the extension registry in its constructor, so the startup
restore is covered too. resolve("include/basestyle.css") now yields the
jar: URL of the real file; it is not a plain file, so the engine keeps the
devstyle: URL it already built and the import still goes through DevStyle's
color-substituting handler — the behavior the old weaver produced. On 4.40
the extra locator is inert for the same reason.

Target: com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css 2025.2.0.202509301431 (resource
patch — plugin.xml is repacked from work/, no compilation involved)
Context source: the bundle's own plugin.xml. Details: docs/css-import-locator.md

--- a/com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css/plugin.xml
+++ b/com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css/plugin.xml
@@ -25,6 +25,16 @@
          <themeid	
                refid="org.eclipse.e4.ui.css.theme.e4_dark">	
          </themeid>	
+         <!-- revstyle: lets the e4 CSS engine resolve the relative @import
+              rules of the DevStyle base stylesheets (include/basestyle.css
+              etc.). Eclipse 2026-09 (4.41) rewrote the engine; its import
+              fallback asks the resource locators and crashes on a null
+              answer, dropping the whole stylesheet. Locators declared here
+              are registered when the engine is built, so even the startup
+              theme restore is covered. -->
+         <osgiresourcelocator
+               uri="platform:/plugin/com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css/css/">
+         </osgiresourcelocator>
 	  </stylesheet>	
    </extension>
 </plugin>
